    {
      "id": "2070843224495960527",
      "text": "Typically when you use coding agents like Claude or Codex you manually prompt and guide the agent to the goal, repeatedly (unless the task can be one-shotted). Loops are essentially workflows designed to take the human out of the loop and guide the agent to the goal autonomously without repeated manual prompting. The most primitive loop is the Ralph loop https://t.co/tSK8xoLk4u or /goal.",
