    {
      "id": "2070091064778621229",
      "text": "Wrapping up with a few easy-to-forget fundamentals:\n\n🟣 Always build the foundation first. When one part of the task drives everything downstream (e.g., data ingest shape, storage schema), getting it right early saves you from a last-minute rewrite of the whole codebase.\n\n🟣 Never give the agent production access. Give it a copy with full context and control, where any mistake is easy to reset. For Superbank, we've used git worktrees and a virtualised cluster.\n\n🟣 Write directional pseudocode and let the agent type it out. Once you know the shape, getting it into syntax is grunt work you can offload.\n\n🟣 Throw your hardest task at every new model. AI moves nearly as fast as @solana, so staying loyal to what worked two months ago puts you behind. Fable 5 one-shotted a new Superbank feature the day it dropped.",
      "author": {
        "id": "1424554867255758850",
        "name": "Triton One 🌊🌋",
        "screenName": "triton_one",
