    {
      "id": "2069518693139435882",
      "text": "Boris Cherny, head of Claude Code:\n\n\"I actually just ran out of hard problems to give it.\"\n\nevery problem he fed the newest model got one-shotted - he couldn't invent a harder one.\n\nand he practices what he preaches: 100% of his code written by AI since Opus 4. ~1,700 PRs this year, 8 billion tokens since March, most of it prompted from his phone.\n\nhis point: coding is no longer the bottleneck. engineers are now bottlenecked on good ideas.\n\n~40-min fireside, free. the head of Claude Code on what's left for humans to do ↓",
      "author": {
        "id": "1686744883556474880",
        "name": "Clodex",
        "screenName": "0xClodex",
        "profileImageUrl": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2054522025314496512/l2XQl34R_normal.jpg",
        "verified": true
